course: dictionary
lesson: 1087
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is meant by reading the words around it, which is its context. «In Melbourne, Tasha can't afford a birthday present and makes a friendship bracelet; the birthday girl wears it all day.» Here a bracelet is a band of thread or beads worn on the wrist as decoration, because Tasha makes it and the girl wears it.
explain: A bracelet can also be a band worn for a purpose. A medical alert bracelet tells people about an allergy or illness, and a hospital wristband tells staff who you are. The clue is the job the band does, not how it looks.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. A friendship bracelet is jewellery, so the decoration meaning fits. A medical bracelet keeps you safe, so the purpose meaning fits.
fact: A bracelet is a band or chain worn around the wrist.
fact: A bracelet can be jewellery or decoration, like a friendship bracelet made from thread or beads.
fact: A bracelet can also be worn for a purpose, like a medical alert bracelet or a hospital wristband.
fact: In maths and art, bead bracelets are used to make repeating patterns.
fact: Bracelet is a noun: one bracelet, two bracelets.
exercise: «Tasha can't afford a present, so she makes a friendship bracelet from thread.» What kind of bracelet is this? | A band worn only to tell doctors about an allergy | A chain used to lock a bike | *A band of thread worn as decoration | A hospital wristband for safety
exercise: A nurse says, «Please wear your medical bracelet, it tells doctors about your allergy.» What is the bracelet for? | *It warns doctors about an allergy | It is a decoration made of beads | It is a hard chain for climbing | It is only for a birthday party
exercise: «A bracelet sold for £1 that cost 20p makes 80p, so 10 sold make £8.» How much profit does one bracelet make? | 20p | £1 | *80p | £8
test: In maths and art, bead bracelets are used to show what? | Pictures of animals | Prices in shops | *Repeating patterns | Weights for measuring
test: Which bracelet is worn for safety, not just decoration? | Thread bracelet bought at a fair | *Medical alert bracelet | Friendship bracelet | Bead bracelet from a shop
exam: In the sentence «The nurse checked the hospital wristband, which is a kind of bracelet.» what does bracelet mean? | A chain for holding keys | Jewellery made of gold | *A band worn for a purpose, like identification | A sweet shaped like a ring
